INT. FAMILY HOUSEBOAT - GALLEY - EVENING

The houseboat rocks in a slow, patient rhythm against the canal wall. A copper lamp swings from a hook. Steam rises from a pot of lentils, fogging the small round window. Dinner is set for four on a table too small for it.

HENRIKA DOLAN (60s, gray braid, forearms dusted with flour) ladles soup without looking up. Across from her sits her son, PIETER DOLAN (35, pressed shirt, a man who has practiced a speech in a mirror). Beside him, his wife ANNELIES (33, careful hands, folding and refolding a napkin).

At the end of the table, an empty chair. A folded newspaper rests on its seat.

HENRIKA
Eat while it's hot.

PIETER
Mama, we need to talk about the boat.

HENRIKA
We are talking. Over soup. It's the best way.

Annelies lays her spoon down with exact quiet.

ANNELIES
The buyer is serious, Henrika.

HENRIKA
There is always a buyer. Last year there was a buyer.

PIETER
Papa's been gone two years.

Henrika's ladle stops. A single drop of soup falls and spreads on the cloth.

HENRIKA
I know how long.

PIETER
Then you know we can't keep paying for the mooring --

HENRIKA
I know what we pay.

A knock at the hull. The door opens. A STRANGER (40s, rain-soaked coat, a canvas satchel) stands on the gangway, hat in hand.

STRANGER
Forgive me. I was told Anders Dolan lived here.

Nobody breathes. Henrika sets the ladle down.

HENRIKA
Who told you that?

STRANGER
A man in Rotterdam. He said to bring this.

He sets a brass compass on the table. Pieter stares at it. Annelies covers her mouth.

HENRIKA
Where did you get that?

STRANGER
My name is Casimir Rooke. Your husband sailed with me, ma'am. Eleven years ago, off Terschelling.

PIETER
Eleven years? He was home eleven years ago.

CASIMIR
Was he?

Henrika walks to the window and presses her palm to the cold glass. The lamp keeps swinging.

HENRIKA
(low)
Sit down, Mr. Rooke. Annelies, a bowl.

PIETER
Mama, no. Not now.

HENRIKA
Pieter, hush.

PIETER
You don't even know who he is!

He stands so fast his chair crashes backward. The soup trembles in its pot.

PIETER (CONT'D)
Two years! Two years you let us believe he drowned clean!

HENRIKA
Sit down.

PIETER
I will not sit down in his house, with his stranger, eating his lentils!

Annelies reaches for his sleeve. He shakes her off. Casimir sets the satchel on the floor and does not move, a man who has walked into a fire he cannot put out.

CASIMIR
He asked me to tell you he was sorry.

Henrika turns. For a long moment, only the water speaks against the hull.
